    <statement><p>Find an equation of a plane through the point (5, -4, -5)
which is orthogonal to the line 
<me>x = 4 + 3t, \quad y = -3
+ 1t, \quad  z = 3 + 2t</me> in which the coefficient of 
<m>x</m> is 3.</p>
<p>Equation: <fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\mathopen{}\left(x-5\right)+1\mathopen{}\left(y-\left(-4\right)\right)+2\mathopen{}\left(z-\left(-5\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
